            <ArticleTitle>[Morphologic investigations on experimental coronary thromboses in pigs (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>293-302</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With the aid of a standardized method basing on a report of Salazar (1961) coronary thromboses in pigs were produced by means of electric induction without opening the chest. 12 of 13 pigs showed thromboses in coronary arteries, in 8 animals with embolization of the thrombotic material. At the sametime in 8 pigs a myocardial infarction could be registered. The significance of these experiments discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
